{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792489599,"nonce":"l7Ih5kHqvOqgWyyMgpXyX+/QFfk=","title":"Layer groups lose isolation when their children are routed into separate batches","message":"While fixing 01a8815bb197768d32d0687a5fcbea81307e5fa540485857e54fb6460700cecf, confirmed that GpuPaintContext::push_layer/pop_layer always record commands in the background batch. Primitive emission can instead target dynamic_batch, a per-node composite scratch batch, or foreground_primitives. bg_layer_command_count and the application animation metadata also assume the background command array.\n\nA minimal emitted-data reproduction: push LayerConfig opacity 0.5; push_motion_subtree; fill two overlapping opaque rectangles; pop_motion_subtree; pop_layer. The background batch has an empty Push/Pop range; the dynamic batch has the rectangles at alpha 0.5 and no layer commands. dispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay dispatches only its primitive slice, so the group has per-child fading rather than isolated group opacity. The composite bake similarly renders a primitive range without walking group commands. Foreground and late images have separate dispatches; z-layer splitting can construct partial batches without the original command ranges. These are source/emitted-data findings, not a claim of newly reproduced end-to-end application pixels.\n\nThe producer-opacity fix deliberately preserves the existing flattened effective opacity on independently dispatched motion/composite/foreground streams and late images, while removing duplicate group alpha from the full background batch. Blindly removing that fallback makes independently dispatched content opaque. The new producer_opacity CPU regressions pin both contracts and route restoration.\n\nA follow-up needs coordinated command ownership, range rebasing, dispatch and cached animation-index changes. Group opacity must be applied after overlapping children are drawn; simply moving commands to active_batch_mut or multiplying primitive alpha is insufficient. Keep this separate from auxiliary-buffer ownership (5571d817c0d8c5003fc2f0c6f4b1928596a2ace51d4f247469e234f20741ed16), the already-fixed native MSAA layer walker (5c9ff267e5f19ea41e0d9e28404a954b7bf2fa092cbdc6abef731a98001321d4), and the late-image clip/order issue (369499d).","files":null}]}